# Vectis Mail Server — Rspamd global Redis (Valkey) connection
# Generated by config engine — do not edit manually
#
# Global backend for every Redis-dependent rspamd module. Without this file
# rspamd logs "Modules disabled (no Redis): history_redis, neural, greylist,
# ratelimit, url_redirector, replies" and silently runs without them; only the
# Bayes classifier (classifier-bayes.conf has its own servers line) worked.
# Found 2026-10-04 on both production boxes: greylisting, including the Pro
# per-domain greylisting control, had never actually run.
#
# Modules this enables are gated individually: greylist by
# rspamd.greylist_enabled (greylist.conf), while neural and url_redirector are
# switched off in the image (docker/rspamd/override.d).
servers = "valkey:6379";
password = "{{ .Valkey.Password }}";
timeout = 2s;
